<article class="env-example" id="02PS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02PS">Example <span data-tag="02PS">42.68.22</span>.</a> Let $R = k$ be a field. Let $M = k^{\oplus a} \oplus k^{\oplus a}$ be $l = 2a$ dimensional. Let $\varphi $ and $\psi $ be the following block matrices </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varphi = \left( \begin{matrix}  0 

&  U 

\\  0 

&  0 

\end{matrix} \right), \quad \psi = \left( \begin{matrix}  0 

&  V 

\\  0 

&  0 

\end{matrix} \right),  \]
</div>
  <p> with $U, V \in \text{Mat}(a \times a, k)$ invertible. In this case we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \det \nolimits _ k(M, \varphi , \psi ) = (-1)^ a\frac{\det (U)}{\det (V)}.  \]
</div>
  <p> This can be seen by a direct computation. The case $a = 1$ is similar to the computation in Example <a href="/tag/02PP" data-tag="02PP">42.68.19</a>. </p>
</article>